## User

The depth of a tree: 0 for a leaf, and one more than the deeper subtree for a node.

## Context

```haskell
data Tree a = Leaf | Node (Tree a) a (Tree a)
```

## Type

type
```haskell
depth :: Tree a -> Int
```

## Term

```haskell
depth (Leaf) = 0
depth (Node l _ r) = 1 + max (depth l) (depth r)
```

